# fan_en_b: The heat-sink fan, handed to the PS. Unless a design puts a port of its own on A12, the board wrapper drives it from the PS8's TTC0 waveform output 2 (EMIO), passed straight through the PL. That is how AMD's platforms and examples/tokenizer wire it (kria_fan.v: assign fout = fin[2]), so Linux's pwm-fan runs the fan and slows it when it is not needed. Without this, a PL-only bitstream takes the fan away from the OS. See the fan device. On silicon 2026-11-03: see the fan device.
set_property LOC A12 [get_ports {fan_en_b}]
set_property IOSTANDARD LVCMOS33 [get_ports {fan_en_b}]

